  "limits": [
    "The requests are driven in-process over ASGITransport, so the application's lifespan never runs. The script therefore installs the logging configuration itself, and asserts that the bound logger is a LevelAwareBoundLogger -- without that the predicate would be structurally always True and every assertion here would be vacuous.",
    "The server-side clock is absent unless REQUEST_TIMER_ENABLED was set when the application was constructed; the reason for its absence is recorded per request rather than papered over. No latency threshold is applied to either clock.",
    "The attack-detection mode is read from the running configuration, so a deployment configured for 'log' or 'ban' is reported on its own terms rather than being forced into 'block'."
  ]
